{
 "component": "BatteryIndicator",
 "version": 1,
 "summary": "A horizontal battery icon filled to a level (0..100) and coloured by it (green, amber below warnAt, red with a ! below lowAt), with an optional percentage.",
 "params": {
  "level": {
   "type": "float",
   "required": true,
   "doc": "Charge in percent, 0..100 (clamped): a number, or a host variable such as \"@battery\" (exported in resources.variables). The format has no system battery value the Java parser accepts, so the host sets it"
  },
  "size": {
   "type": "float",
   "default": 40,
   "static": true,
   "doc": "Icon width in dp; the icon is half as tall (the design size: it shrinks to a smaller box)"
  },
  "showPercent": {
   "type": "bool",
   "default": true,
   "static": true,
   "doc": "Write the level as \"76%\" after the icon"
  },
  "fontSize": {
   "type": "float",
   "default": 13,
   "static": true,
   "doc": "Size of the percentage, in sp"
  },
  "warnAt": {
   "type": "float",
   "default": 50,
   "doc": "Below this the fill is @colors.warning"
  },
  "lowAt": {
   "type": "float",
   "default": 20,
   "doc": "Below this the fill is @colors.error and a ! is drawn in the empty part"
  },
  "label": {
   "type": "string",
   "default": "Battery",
   "doc": "Accessibility label of the icon"
  }
 },
 "locals": {
  "lv": "clamp(0, 100, @level)"
 },
 "capabilities": [
  "draw.shapes",
  "data.condition",
  "text.dynamic",
  "host.variables"
 ],
 "call": {
  "BatteryIndicator": {
   "level": "@battery"
  }
 },
 "body": {
  "row": {
   "verticalAlignment": "center",
   "modifiers": [
    {
     "spacedBy": "@theme.space_1 + 2"
    }
   ],
   "children": [
    {
     "canvas": {
      "modifiers": [
       {
        "width": "@size"
       },
       {
        "height": "@size * 0.5"
       },
       {
        "semantics": {
         "contentDescription": "@label"
        }
       }
      ],
      "commands": [
       {
        "variable": {
         "name": "k",
         "value": "min(componentWidth() / @size, componentHeight() / (@size * 0.5))"
        }
       },
       {
        "translate": {
         "dx": "(componentWidth() - @size * @k) / 2",
         "dy": "(componentHeight() - @size * 0.5 * @k) / 2"
        }
       },
       {
        "scale": {
         "sx": "@k",
         "sy": "@k"
        }
       },
       {
        "paint": {
         "ops": [
          {
           "color": "@colors.muted"
          },
          {
           "style": "stroke"
          },
          {
           "strokeWidth": "@theme.stroke"
          }
         ]
        }
       },
       {
        "drawRoundRect": {
         "left": 1,
         "top": 1,
         "right": "@size * 0.88 - 1",
         "bottom": "@size * 0.5 - 1",
         "rx": "@size * 0.1",
         "ry": "@size * 0.1"
        }
       },
       {
        "paint": {
         "ops": [
          {
           "style": "fill"
          }
         ]
        }
       },
       {
        "drawRoundRect": {
         "left": "@size * 0.88 + 1",
         "top": "@size * 0.16",
         "right": "@size",
         "bottom": "@size * 0.34",
         "rx": "@size * 0.04",
         "ry": "@size * 0.04"
        }
       },
       {
        "paint": {
         "ops": [
          {
           "color": "@colors.success"
          }
         ]
        }
       },
       {
        "conditionalOperations": {
         "condition": "lt",
         "v1": "@lv",
         "v2": "@warnAt",
         "commands": [
          {
           "paint": {
            "ops": [
             {
              "color": "@colors.warning"
             }
            ]
           }
          }
         ]
        }
       },
       {
        "conditionalOperations": {
         "condition": "lt",
         "v1": "@lv",
         "v2": "@lowAt",
         "commands": [
          {
           "paint": {
            "ops": [
             {
              "color": "@colors.error"
             }
            ]
           }
          },
          {
           "drawRoundRect": {
            "left": "@size * 0.44 - 1.25",
            "top": "@size * 0.12",
            "right": "@size * 0.44 + 1.25",
            "bottom": "@size * 0.29",
            "rx": 1.25,
            "ry": 1.25
           }
          },
          {
           "drawCircle": {
            "cx": "@size * 0.44",
            "cy": "@size * 0.36",
            "radius": 1.4
           }
          }
         ]
        }
       },
       {
        "drawRoundRect": {
         "left": 4,
         "top": 4,
         "right": "4 + (@size * 0.88 - 8) * @lv / 100",
         "bottom": "@size * 0.5 - 4",
         "rx": "@size * 0.1 - 3",
         "ry": "@size * 0.1 - 3"
        }
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "$if": "showPercent",
     "then": {
      "text": {
       "value": {
        "type": "textMerge",
        "id1": {
         "type": "textFromFloat",
         "value": "@lv",
         "whole": 3,
         "decimal": 0,
         "flags": 4
        },
        "id2": "%"
       },
       "fontSize": "@fontSize",
       "color": "@colors.onSurface"
      }
     }
    }
   ]
  }
 },
 "pitfalls": [
  "There is no portable system battery level: batteryLevel() (system variable 38) is an rcj/json2rc extension that the Java parser rejects and Android's RemoteContext does not define. Export a host float (resources.variables {\"battery\": {\"value\": 76, \"export\": true}}) and pass \"@battery\"; the host updates it",
  "The fill colour is chosen with conditionalOperations around a paint change (success, then warning below warnAt, then error below lowAt): there are no colour expressions",
  "Low is shown by shape too: a ! in the empty part of the body, so it reads in mono (where every colour is white or black) and without colour vision",
  "The percentage is a layout text after the icon, so the call is as wide as the icon plus the number: in a tight row, pass showPercent: false and show the level elsewhere",
  "The icon is scaled to the box the layout gives its canvas (the smaller of width / size and height / (size / 2), centred), so a call clamped by a smaller parent shrinks instead of being cut off; the outline stays theme.stroke wide at the design size and scales with it"
 ]
}
